# The vendored dependencies are byte-exact on purpose.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for this repo, which is right for source I edit and wrong
# for these: a checkout that rewrote their line endings would change their SIZE,
# and web/VENDOR.md records byte counts that tests/test_web_assets.py checks
# against the disk. A fresh clone would then fail a test for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the code -- and on the Oracle box the files would differ
# from this machine's for the same non-reason.
#
# `-text` means "never convert". The bytes that were fetched are the bytes that
# are served, on every platform.
web/vendor/** -text
